  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196800: Bounded PostgreSQL extended batch pipeline

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

`pg_execute_batch` accepts a bounded descriptor containing up to eight named
statements and their independently validated typed parameter fragments. The
provider reconstructs one Bind and Execute pair per item and emits exactly one
Sync after the final item. Consumers cannot inject arbitrary frontend message
types or additional Sync boundaries through the descriptor.

On success, the response must contain one BindComplete and one CommandComplete
per item and terminate at ReadyForQuery. PostgreSQL's error-until-Sync behavior
is preserved: an ErrorResponse may terminate the remaining item responses, but
must carry bounded SQLSTATE metadata and be followed by ReadyForQuery before
the session is reused. Descriptor count, name, parameter fragment, aggregate
length and exact exhaustion are checked before the first write.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification executes two prepared `select 42`
statements through one Sync and observes two rows. A three-item batch succeeds
on item one, fails with `22012` on item two, proves item three is ignored until
Sync, then successfully executes a new batch on the same affine session.

This closes the bounded single-connection batch pipeline slice. Cross-session
multiplexing, connection pooling, rotation, compatibility matrices and soak
remain open."}]
